#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, create a minimal environment with only Python installed in it. We "
"recommend using [Python virtual "
"environments](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate your new environment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are two primary ways to install this package: from PyPI or from "
"source. The preferred method is to install from PyPI:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install from PyPI {#install-from-pypi}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install from source {#install-from-source}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you plan to develop in the repository or run the notebooks locally, you "
"should install from source.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First, clone the `qiskit-paulice` repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, install the Rust toolchain, upgrade pip, and enter the repository. "
"Refer to the [Rust documentation](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install) "
"for instructions on installing the toolchain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The next step is to install `qiskit-paulice` to the virtual environment. If "
"you plan to run the notebooks and their visualizations, install the notebook"
" dependencies. If you plan on developing in the repository, install the "
"`dev` dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adjust the options below to suit your needs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you installed the notebook dependencies, you can get started by running "
"the notebooks in the docs.\n"
msgstr ""
